## Expression binding
Inline expressions con `{= ... }`:

### Comparación
```xml
<Text text='{= ${Price} > 100 ? 'Expensive' : 'Cheap' }'/>
<Icon src='{= ${Status} === 'Active' ? 'sap-icon://accept' : 'sap-icon://decline' }'/>
<Button visible='{= ${Role} === 'Admin' }' text='Admin Only'/>
```

### Aritmética
```xml
<Text text='{= ${Price} * ${Quantity} }'/>
<Text text='{= ${Total} - ${Discount} }'/>
```

### String
```xml
<Text text='{= ${FirstName} + ' ' + ${LastName} }'/>
<Text text='{= ${Name}.toUpperCase() }'/>
```

### Boolean
```xml
<Button enabled='{= ${Amount} > 0 && ${Status} !== 'Closed' }'/>
```

### Multiple paths
```xml
<Text text='{= ${FirstName} + ' ' + ${LastName} + ' (' + ${Age} + ' años)' }'/>
```

## Formatters (más complex logic)

### Definir en controller
```javascript
sap.ui.define([
    'sap/ui/core/mvc/Controller'
], function(Controller) {
    return Controller.extend('com.empresa.miapp.controller.Main', {
        formatter: {
            price: function(value) {
                if (value == null) return '';
                return new Intl.NumberFormat('es-CO', {
                    style: 'currency',
                    currency: 'COP'
                }).format(value);
            },

            statusIcon: function(status) {
                switch (status) {
                    case 'Active': return 'sap-icon://accept';
                    case 'Blocked': return 'sap-icon://error';
                    case 'Pending': return 'sap-icon://pending';
                    default: return 'sap-icon://question-mark';
                }
            },

            formatDate: function(date) {
                if (!date) return '';
                return new Date(date).toLocaleDateString('es-CO');
            }
        }
    });
});
```

### Uso en view
```xml
<Text text='{ path: 'Price', formatter: '.formatter.price' }'/>
<Icon src='{ path: 'Status', formatter: '.formatter.statusIcon' }'/>
<Text text='{ path: 'CreatedAt', formatter: '.formatter.formatDate' }'/>
```

## Composite binding
```xml
<Text text='{
    parts: [
        { path: 'FirstName' },
        { path: 'LastName' },
        { path: 'Age' }
    ],
    formatter: '.formatter.fullName'
}'/>
```

```javascript
fullName: function(first, last, age) {
    return `${first} ${last} (${age})`;
}
```

## Built-in types con constraints y formatOptions
```xml
<Input value='{
    path: 'Amount',
    type: 'sap.ui.model.type.Currency',
    constraints: { minimum: 0 },
    formatOptions: { showMeasure: true, currencyCode: false }
}'/>

<Text text='{
    path: 'BirthDate',
    type: 'sap.ui.model.type.Date',
    formatOptions: { style: 'medium' }
}'/>

<Text text='{
    path: 'Percentage',
    type: 'sap.ui.model.type.Float',
    formatOptions: { style: 'percent', decimals: 2 }
}'/>

<Input value='{
    path: 'Email',
    type: 'sap.ui.model.type.String',
    constraints: { search: '^\\S+@\\S+\\.\\S+$' }
}'/>
```

## Two-way binding
Inputs by default two-way — user changes propagate to model:
```xml
<Input value='{Name}'/>
```

User types 'John' → `oModel.getProperty('/Name')` returns 'John' automatically.

## One-time binding
Only evaluated once:
```xml
<Text text='{ path: 'CreatedAt', mode: 'OneTime' }'/>
```

## Binding modes
- **OneWay** (default for property) — model → UI only
- **TwoWay** — bidirectional (Inputs)
- **OneTime** — read once

```javascript
oModel.setDefaultBindingMode(sap.ui.model.BindingMode.TwoWay);
```

## Custom types
Extend `sap.ui.model.SimpleType` para reusable custom validators.

## OPA5 (One Page Acceptance)
UI5 built-in testing framework para functional UI tests.

## Structure
```
webapp/
  test/
    opaTests.qunit.html      # test runner
    opaTests.qunit.js
    integration/
      arrangements/
        Startup.js           # setup
      pages/
        Main.js              # page object model
      journeys/
        MainJourney.js       # test scenarios
```

## Startup (arrangements)
```javascript
// test/integration/arrangements/Startup.js
sap.ui.define(['sap/ui/test/Opa5'], function(Opa5) {
    return Opa5.extend('com.empresa.miapp.test.arrangements.Startup', {
        iStartMyApp: function() {
            return this.iStartMyUIComponent({
                componentConfig: {
                    name: 'com.empresa.miapp',
                    async: true
                }
            });
        }
    });
});
```

## Page object model
```javascript
// test/integration/pages/Main.js
sap.ui.define([
    'sap/ui/test/Opa5',
    'sap/ui/test/matchers/PropertyStrictEquals'
], function(Opa5, PropertyStrictEquals) {
    Opa5.createPageObjects({
        onTheMainPage: {
            actions: {
                iPressSaveButton: function() {
                    return this.waitFor({
                        controlType: 'sap.m.Button',
                        matchers: new PropertyStrictEquals({
                            name: 'text',
                            value: 'Save'
                        }),
                        actions: function(oButton) {
                            oButton.$().trigger('tap');
                        },
                        errorMessage: 'Save button not found'
                    });
                }
            },

            assertions: {
                iShouldSeeSuccessMessage: function() {
                    return this.waitFor({
                        controlType: 'sap.m.MessageToast',
                        success: function() {
                            Opa5.assert.ok(true, 'Success shown');
                        },
                        errorMessage: 'No success message'
                    });
                }
            }
        }
    });
});
```

## Journey (test scenario)
```javascript
sap.ui.define([
    'sap/ui/test/Opa5',
    'com/empresa/miapp/test/arrangements/Startup',
    'com/empresa/miapp/test/integration/pages/Main'
], function(Opa5, Startup, Main) {
    Opa5.extendConfig({ arrangements: new Startup() });

    QUnit.module('Save flow');

    opaTest('User can save form', function(Given, When, Then) {
        Given.iStartMyApp();

        When.onTheMainPage.iPressSaveButton();

        Then.onTheMainPage.iShouldSeeSuccessMessage();
    });
});
```

## Run tests
### Local
```bash
npm run test:opa
# Or:
npx karma start
```

Opens browser, runs tests.

### CI
```bash
npx karma start --single-run --browsers Chrome_no_sandbox
```

Headless Chrome for CI.

## Matchers
- **PropertyStrictEquals** — exact match property value
- **BindingPath** — control bound to specific path
- **I18NText** — text matches i18n key
- **Ancestor** — child of specific control
- **Descendant**

## Actions
- **Press** — click
- **EnterText** — type
- **Drag / Drop**
- Custom via `actions: function(oControl) {}`

## Best practices
- **Page objects** para reusability
- **Meaningful test names**
- **One assertion per test** ideal
- **Clean up** between tests (restart component or reset state)
- **Wait strategies** — use `waitFor` (auto-waits UI ready)

## Coverage
OPA5 + code coverage tool:
```bash
npm install --save-dev karma-coverage
```

Configure en karma.conf.js. Generates coverage report.

## Debug tests
- Add `debugger;` en test
- Run en headed browser (not headless)
- Step through en DevTools

## Common issues
- **Timeout errors** — increase `waitFor` timeout
- **Control not found** — element not rendered yet, adjust matchers
- **Flaky tests** — timing issues, add explicit waits

## Fiori Elements V4
Generation nueva basada en OData v4:
- Better developer experience
- Faster runtime
- Draft handling native
- Improved annotations

## Templates supported
- **List Report** (with V4)
- **Object Page**
- **Analytical List Page**
- **Overview Page**

## Requerimientos
- OData v4 backend
- SAPUI5 1.99+
- Manifest.json con `sap.ui5.dependencies.libs`: `sap.fe.templates`

## Create con BAS wizard
**Fiori Application** → **List Report Object Page** → **OData v4**.

## Diferencias vs V2 Fiori Elements

### Deep pattern
V4 provides deeper integration with OData semantics.

### Draft management
Built-in:
- Auto-save every N seconds
- Discard changes button
- Publish (activate) flow

### Actions
```cds
action discount(percent: Integer) returns Product;
action cancelOrder() returns Order;
```

Appear as buttons in UI automatically.

### Determined vs bound actions
- **Bound** — action on specific entity (right-click row → action)
- **Unbound** — global action (button in toolbar)

## Manifest.json for FE V4
```json
{
    'sap.ui5': {
        'rootView': {
            'viewName': 'sap.fe.templates.ListReport.ListReport',
            'type': 'XML'
        },
        'dependencies': {
            'libs': {
                'sap.fe.templates': {}
            }
        },
        'routing': {
            'routes': [
                {
                    'pattern': ':?query:',
                    'name': 'ProductList',
                    'target': 'ProductList'
                }
            ],
            'targets': {
                'ProductList': {
                    'type': 'Component',
                    'name': 'sap.fe.templates.ListReport',
                    'options': {
                        'settings': {
                            'entitySet': 'Products',
                            'variantManagement': 'Page'
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## CAP integration
CAP CDS annotations map directly to Fiori Elements V4:

```cds
// srv/service.cds
service CatalogService {
    entity Products as projection on my.Products;
}

annotate CatalogService.Products with @(
    UI: {
        HeaderInfo: {
            TypeName: 'Product',
            Title: { Value: name }
        },
        LineItem: [
            { Value: name },
            { Value: price },
            { Value: stock }
        ],
        Facets: [
            { $Type: 'UI.ReferenceFacet', Label: 'General', Target: '@UI.FieldGroup#Main' }
        ],
        FieldGroup #Main: {
            Data: [
                { Value: description },
                { Value: category }
            ]
        }
    }
);
```

CAP + FE V4 = powerful combo for CRUD apps.

## Advantages of FE V4
- **Less code** — annotations drive UI
- **Faster** — optimized OData v4 client
- **Better UX** — modern patterns built-in
- **Draft** — auto-save native

## Extension points
Custom sections, actions, fields via extensions:
```javascript
sap.ui.define(['sap/fe/core/AppComponent'], function(AppComponent) {
    return AppComponent.extend('com.empresa.miapp.Component', {
        // Custom hooks
    });
});
```

## Custom UI elements
Most customization via annotations. For truly custom UI → freestyle (not FE).

## Migration V2 → V4 Fiori Elements
- Backend must support OData v4
- Manifest template changes
- Extensions rewritten

Non-trivial. Plan effort.

## Roadmap
FE V4 is future. SAP focuses on it. V2 still supported but new features go to V4.
